ent of linguistics , are the publishers of COPiL . If you meant to ask who our * printer * is , then we 're using some printer 's on the &NAME Street ( &NAME could n't remember the name ! ) . ) Anyway , &NAME said that sure , we could publish your proceedings . As long as the papers are kept to a maximum of &NAME , then &NAME suggested we could put out a 2-volume proceedings . However , as we ( the department / &NAME ) might not make any money on it , we 'd have to get the &NAME conference to fund the initial expense , he said . If , on the other hand , your request was to ask whether we could share the papers themselves , i.e. whether some of your &NAME proceedings papers could be published as part of our first volume of COPiL this year , then no , I 'm afraid we would n't be able to accommodate your conference proceedings within &NAME itself . Firstly , we would n't have the space ( we already have a full line-up of papers for our &NUM volume ) , and secondly , &NAME is meant to showcase work by members of the &NAME linguistics department ( especially our PhD students ) , not people from outside the department ( whose universities probably have their own working papers ! ) &NAME that helps ! Let me know your further thoughts on the matter ... Cheers , &NAME . <END_QUOTE> <END_QUOTE> 
