SUBJECT: Re : [ &NAME ] Working Papers Dear all - -On &NUM &NAME &NUM &NUM : &NUM &NUM " &NAME &NAME " ( &EMAIL ) wrote : <QUOTE> Hi everybody , Just to let you know my feelings on the matters under discussion . Firstly , it seems that we need another meeting soon so that we can take some crucial decisions . As to our publisher , I think that we should first try to publish the proceedings without depending on the Working Papers , because it would seem as if the conference is organized by the Department and in any case , I think it better to emphasize the across-the-board Linguistics of the conference , instead of publishing in Working papers of a particular department . As to our policy , I think we should ideally include all papers , all the more so because the proceedings wo n't be published by a " big " publisher as &NAME , and there might be problems concerning the selection of papers . <END_QUOTE> I definitely agree with the thrust of this whole message but this sentence contains a problem I think . Yes , we want to emphasise the across-the-board Linguistics of the conference , so it would be ideal to be able to publish all the papers , but I do n't think we would be able to afford to do this ourselves ( if anyone can prove me wrong , I 'd welcome it ! ) . Getting help from &NAME &NAME &NAME as the editor of the Linguistics Working Papers may be the way to do this . ( This need n't necessarily mean that they published them ; &NAME might be able just to give us some hints about how to get it done cheaply . &NAME had also said that it might be possible , with their help , to publish &NUM volumes , so that , if we go down the route of including all the papers in the publication , this might be the only way to do it . We certainly would n't be able to afford to publish &NUM volumes on our own . ) Also , I return to the point that &NAME &NAME and &NAME &NAME made to me about wanting to publish only * good * papers , not anything we get just because it has been submitted . We want there to be a quality product in the end . I recognise that we then have the problem of how to select what is published and what is n't, but I think that any academic staff member that we asked for advice or help on this would agree with them and me . &NAME used the example of ( &CHAR ) bad apple ( &CHAR ) in a barrel dragging down the impression that you get of the whole barrel . I think &NAME 's right that we need to meet to make a decision on what we are going to publish ; preferably when we 're armed with figures etc to help us decide ! I can arrange to be free at most times , with a bit of notice , but I obviously prefer meetings to be short ! See you all soon , maybe , then . All the best &NAME 
